  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/gen400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Gen 406.13 Teaching Genetic Counseling",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Gen 406.13 Teaching Genetic Counseling.\n\n(a) The licensee shall receive continuing professional education credit for teaching a college or university course in genetic counseling.\n\n(b) The licensee shall receive 2 hours of continuing professional education credit for each clock hour of teaching, to a maximum of 8 hours per renewal cycle, provided that:\n\n(1) If the licensee gives substantially the same course more than once during the renewal cycle, the board shall credit the licensee for only a single presentation of the course; and\n\n(2) If the licensee gives a course that includes a lab component, the board shall credit the licensee for only a single presentation of the course.\n\n(c) Documentation of genetic counseling teaching shall be:\n\n(1) A list of courses taught; and\n\n(2) A photocopy of a letter of confirmation signed by an official of the institution sponsoring the courses.\n\nSource. #10687, eff 10-7-14; ss by #13556, eff 4-11-23 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Gen 400); ss by #14338, eff 10-7-25, EXPIRES: 10-7-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/gen400.html"
